{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Israel did e[Eb]vil in the sight of the [Cm]Lord
Hand[Ab]ed over to Midian for seven [Bbsus4]long years
[Bb]They hid in [Eb]caves and strongholds in [Cm]the mountains
Crops de[Ab]stroyed and livestock [Bbsus4]taken a[Eb]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Ab]Crying out to the Lord [Cm]in their distress
[Ab]Gideon heard the [Bbsus4]call to [Bb]fight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
A sword for [Eb]the Lord and for Gideon
Three hundred [Cm]men with trumpets sounding
[Ab]Smashing the jars and lighting the torches
The [Bb]army fled in panic and fear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Messengers sent to the hill country of Ep[Cm]hraim
Seize the [Ab]waters ahead of the enemy
[Bb]Capture the two commanders Oreb and [Eb]Zeeb
Killed at the [Ab]rock that [Bb]bears his [Eb]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
A sword for the Lord and for Gideon
Three hundred [Cm]men with trumpets sounding
[Ab]Smashing the jars and lighting the torches
The [Bb]army fled in panic and fear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
